# 0003 XeGfxIntelFB: measure the panel from BAR0 and publish a detailed timing
#
# Base:  NvGfx xe 5a19a73f36249efb99c44c3f9cb34603ef0c0eb8 (XeGfx 0.0.44)
# Files: kexts/XeGfxIntelFB/intelfb.cpp (modified)
#        kexts/XeGfxIntelFB/xe/firmware-timing.h (new)
#        kexts/XeGfxIntelFB/xe/panel-timing.h (new)
#        kexts/XeGfxIntelFB/nvrm-agdc-k5.h (new, copy of the AGDC K5 timing header)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0003-intelfb-panel-timing.patch
#
# The firmware framebuffer describes its mode with no timing, and CoreDisplay only recomputes
# a mode refresh rate when kIODetailedTimingValid is set.  The IONDRVFramebuffer subclass now
# maps BAR0, reads the display-pipe registers and the panel's frame counter for a stable
# snapshot (pixel clock 276,871,248 Hz, 2560x1600 at 59.877 Hz on the test panel), reports that
# refresh rate from getInformationForDisplayMode(), and publishes an IODetailedTimingInformationV2
# from getTimingInfoForDisplayMode() so CoreDisplay can recompute the mode refresh itself.
# The same patch logs where a hardware cursor image could live in the boot aperture.
#

